(what the baseline contains) I asked claude-2 for four things:
1. Counted figures, each with how it was counted:
   - cold runs today and their time;
   - predictions made and how many were right;
   - how many stops moved and how many repeated, and how many dispatch rounds each stop took;
   - tests later found not to have exercised production;
   - my own wrong diagnoses.
2. Each row's current state, in readable terms: what Lean produces, what the port produces, and where they differ.
3. An assessment of the method against Lean as the ground truth: what in it yields correct fixes, and where it lets wrong beliefs through.
4. What a later audit should check to tell whether the method improved.

(limits I set) The audit is read-only:
- claude-2 won't message the Codex agents, edit the worktrees or start builds;
- if it runs the comparator, it does so under the 4G cap;
- I gave it my own transcript and logs to check my claims.
